you keep the first roll only if it beats three and a half, so you keep a four, a five or a six. work it out at home, it comes to four and a quarter.

11
00:04:31,000 --> 00:05:00,000
back to the slides. this is the bellman equation, and it is the heart of the whole course.

12
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:30,000
the value of a state is the immediate reward plus gamma times the <i>expected</i> value of wherever you land next.

13
00:05:30,000 --> 00:06:00,000
the bellman equation is recursive: the value on the left shows up again on the right hand side.

14
